   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 6.4. Increased capacity of ILO constituents to strengthen legislation, polices and measures to ensure equal opportunities and treatment in the world of work for persons with disabilities and other persons in vulnerable situations</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.	Guidelines for modern day workplace policies and programmes developed and adopted by the South African National AIDS Council (SANAC) Legal and Human Rights Technical Task Team (LHR-TTT). The findings of a study conducted to assess the effectiveness and relevance of legislation and policies related to HIV and AIDS in the world of work were adopted by the South African National AIDS Council SANAC LHR-TTT

2.	In August-2020, Business Unity South Africa (BUSA) and the South African Business Coalition on Health and AIDS (SABCOHA) signed a Memorandum of Understanding on implementation of policies and programmes related to HIV/TB, Gender-Based Violence and addressing stigma and discrimination targeted at Persons with Disabilities.

3.	The SANAC Private Sector Forum (SANAC-PSF) was  established and launched by the Deputy President of South Africa in June-11, 2021. The SANAC-PSF, chaired by BUSA and comprised by BUSA and the Black Business Council, formalized a commitment by the private sector to the fight against HIV and AIDS, including discrimination.

4.	The Eastern Cape Department of Health (ECDoH) established a Technical Working Group to address the impact of COVID-19 in relation to Occupational Health and Safety (OHS); Wellness and Disease Management (incl. HIV and AIDS); and Social Dialogue. The TWG is comprised of ECDoH; Department of Employment and Labour (DoEL); Organized Labour (DENOSA; NEHAWU; HOSPERSA; and PSA

5.	Government develops a monitoring and reporting tool in order to capture stigma information related to People Living with HIV (PLHIV), Persons with Disabilities (PWDs), and LGBTIQ+. 1.	The ILO is a member of the SANAC/LHR-TTT, and support is provided to the TTT by participating in the meetings and comment on the relevant documents, including the Human-Rights Plan. The ILO presented the work planned for the assessment of relevance of legislation and policies related to HIV and TB in the workplace.
2.	The ILO provided advice and technical support (training) to the SABCOHA Board of Directors on a continuous basis. The support included the facilitation of the development of the MoU and signing.
3.	The ILO provided financial support through a GRANT in order to support the establishment and launch of the SANAC-PSF-Forum in 11-June 2021.
4.	Upon receiving a request in May-2020, the ILO facilitated consultations with the Provincial Government and Social Partners in the Eastern Cape. The ILO provided continuous technical support by participating in meetings of the Technical Working Group scheduled for every Wednesday since August-2020. The ILO wrote to the Director General of DoEL for the appointment of a Convener for the TWG. The ILO provided financial resources for the TWG to hold its first &#x2018;in-person&apos;
5.	The ILO provided technical and financial ($250,000) support to SABCOHA on areas related to a) Data Mapping and Reporting; b) HIV Testing Services; and c) Establishment of the Private Sector Forum</narrative>
   </description>
